s located in the Valley of the Cross, below the Israel Museum and the Knesset.", "newValue": "The Monastery of the Holy Cross, located in the Valley of the Cross near Jerusalem, stands as a testament to the religious and cultural heritage of the Eastern Orthodox Church. Established in the 4th century CE, its foundation is attributed to Saint Helen, the mother of Emperor Constantine, who sought to erect a place of worship on the site believed to mark the location of the true Cross. As one of the oldest and most significant monastic institutions in the region, it has played a vital role in the spread of Christianity through its educational and spiritual activities, influencing the religious landscape of West Asia.

